The tools/go.mod pattern — a second module kept out of the main build so its
dependencies stay out of go.sum. Extremely common, and the recipe that asks the
module graph misses it exactly as it misses any nested module.

modules_on_disk: 2
go_list_m: 1
go_list_dotdotdot: 1
discovered_modules: 2
discovered_packages: 2
packages_with_tests: 0
-- go.mod --
module fixture.test/app

go 1.27
-- app.go --
package app

func A() int { return 1 }
-- tools/go.mod --
module fixture.test/app/tools

go 1.27
-- tools/tools.go --
package tools

func T() int { return 2 }
